    #   3. the run log's own comparison (shiftcmp.py, python3, zipfile, byte
    #      spans and ElementTree, printed below) over every output of both
    #      labels: W outside the elements the rule names byte-identical; every
    #      cell left of the point byte-identical; sheetData byte for byte the
    #      model's (cells retagged, a deleted column's cells cut out and their
    #      rows kept, spans through the rule, shared, array and data table refs
    #      moved); every cell at its moved reference by ElementTree; every row's
    #      start tag the model's (spans); dimension, mergeCells, cols and the
    #      four lists as the rule gives; the chain and the flag exactly when a
    #      formula sits at or after the point; each tool line's counts against
    #      the comparison's; the refusal set computed from the input and
    #      matched (P2 ruling 6); a planted control per flag; the two labels'
    #      outputs byte for byte;
    #   4. the keep regenerated on both targets, compared, and against P2's
    #      committed open-check record; the edit open check over the host keep,
    #      recorded as m2p3-open-<utc-date>-<shortsha>;
    #   5. this script's own standard error counted (specs/0017 P1 verification
    #      ruling 7).
    # No cell value, text, reference or part name is printed. A bare ruling
    # number in a check below (ruling 6, 11, 13) is one of specs/0018's
    # "Planning rulings during P2".
    #
    # CARRIED TO M2 part 3 P3 from P2's run script (printed in
    # records/logs/m2p3-p2/run.log; its change list K to P is there). What
    # differs, and why:
    #  Q. The phase, the log directory, the script directory <scratch>/p3, the
    #     subjects, the build directory (m2p3-p3-run) and the keep
    #     (m2p3-p3-keep-host) are P3's; the base is P2's record commit ("M2
    #     part 3 P2 record:"); the phase commit is code commit 3 by its
    #     subject; the record stems are m2p3-p3-insert- and m2p3-p3-delete-.
    #  R. The samples are --insert-columns-sample (one column at c) and
    #     --delete-columns-sample (column c), c = max(2, U + 1), U the largest
    #     last column of W's table and pivot ranges. shiftcmp.py gains the
    #     column axis (modes insert-columns and delete-columns; the row modes
    #     kept): its point is c, its rule the column rule of P3 rulings 1 and
    #     2, and its flags on this axis are rest_same, cells_before_same,
    #     sheetdata_bytes, cells_moved, spans_ok, dimension_ok, merges_ok,
    #     cols_ok, lists_ok and calc_ok (rows_before_same is the row axis's).
    #     The tool line's fields are P3 ruling 3's (from_c_before and
    #     from_c1_after; from_c1_before and from_c_after; count 1 both ways),
    #     and line_as_spec reads them.
    #  S. Three corrections to the comparison's model, found while validating
    #     it on generated fixtures before this log: an element written with an
    #     end tag and no content (<row ...></row>, <c ...></c>) keeps its end
    #     tag (P2's model cut it, a form no corpus first sheet held); a
    #     container given as an empty-element tag is copied as it is, as the
    #     library copies it; a table relationship whose part is not there is a
    #     refusal, as the library refuses it (P2 ruling 2). The comparison's
    #     line no longer prints merges_in and lists_in, which no check read.
    #  T. P2 ruling 14: the moved keep's pair count is counted with its
    #     pattern in double quotes, so the tab is interpolated, and a check
