## the run log's comparison (python3, zipfile, byte spans and ElementTree)
command: sed 's/^/    /' <scratch>/w/shiftcmp.py; sha256 c3b1ab91d2d7384104dc827433e17da41e880496701181c2196095e5a3e0d312, 35887 bytes
    """The run log's own shift comparison (specs/0018-rows-and-columns.md,
    "Harness runs", the row samples of P2 and the column samples of P3, with
    "Planning rulings during P2" 1 to 8 and "Planning rulings during P3" 1 to
    3).
    
    Usage: shiftcmp.py <mode> <input archive> <output archive> [--plant <flag>]
           shiftcmp.py <mode> <input archive> --predict
           shiftcmp.py <mode> <input archive> --unchanged
           shiftcmp.py <mode> <input archive> --parts
    <mode> is insert or delete (the row samples: two rows inserted at k, or
    row k deleted) or insert-columns or delete-columns (the column samples: one
    column inserted at c, or column c deleted).
    
    Reads the archives with zipfile, byte spans and ElementTree, sharing no code
    with the library or the tool. It makes its own pick of W (the first
    worksheet in <sheets> order) and of the point: max(2, T + 1), T the largest
    last row (on the column axis U, the largest last column) of the ref of every
    table part and the location ref of every pivot table part W's relationships
    name. From W's input bytes it builds, by "The shift rule" as the P2 and P3
    rulings read it (this script's own model), what W's output must hold.
    Flags on both axes:
    
      rest_same         W with every root child the rule names cut out is the
                        input's: sheetData, dimension, mergeCells,
                        conditionalFormatting, dataValidations, hyperlinks,
                        autoFilter, and on the column axis cols
      sheetdata_bytes   sheetData is byte for byte the model's: on the row axis
                        every row at or after k with r as the rule gives, a
                        deleted row cut out whole; on the column axis every row
                        kept with its spans as the rule gives, a deleted
                        column's cell cut out whole; every cell's r as the rule
                        gives and a shared, array or data table ref moved whole,
                        every other byte the input's
      cells_moved       read with ElementTree, every input cell before the point
                        is in the output at its reference and every one after is
                        at its moved reference, each with the same s, t, formula
                        and value, a deleted cell absent, no other cell
      dimension_ok      dimension as the rule gives, clipped, A1 when emptied
      merges_ok         mergeCells as the rule gives: each ref moved, grown or
                        cut, dropped when removed or reduced to one cell, count
                        its children, the container dropped when emptied
      lists_ok          every conditionalFormatting, dataValidations,
                        hyperlinks and autoFilter element as the rule gives:
                        each range moved or cut, dropped from its list, an
                        element whose list empties dropped with its content,
                        dataValidations' count its children, an emptied
                        dataValidations or hyperlinks dropped
      calc_ok           the output's workbook asks for a full calculation on
                        load exactly when a formula sits at or after the point,
                        and its calculation chain is gone exactly then (when it
                        had one)
    
    On the row axis only:
    
      rows_before_same  sheetData's content before its first row at or after
                        k is the input's, byte for byte
    
    On the column axis only:
    
      cells_before_same every cell element left of c, in document order, is the
                        input's byte for byte
      spans_ok          every row's start tag is the model's: the input's, with
                        spans as P3 ruling 2 gives (each a:b item moved, grown,
                        cut or clipped, an item the rule removes dropped, the
                        attribute dropped when none is left)
      cols_ok           every cols element as the rule gives: each col's min and
                        max moved, grown, cut or clipped at 16384, a col the rule
                        removes dropped, a cols left with no col dropped; order
                        and overlap are not checked (P3 ruling 1)
    
    An input container with no content (an empty-element tag) is copied as it
    is on both axes: the rule leaves nothing in it to drop.
    
    --parts prints W, the workbook part, its rels part and its calculation
    chain part (an empty line when there is none), for the log to match the
    runner's entry rows without printing a name. --unchanged prints whether the
    model leaves W's bytes as the input's (unchanged=yes|no), so the log expects
    W `recompressed` there and `changed` elsewhere (P2 ruling 13). --predict
    prints whether the rule refuses this input (refuse=yes|no) and nothing
    else: a shared, array or data table ref the rule would grow or cut or push
    past the grid, a row or cell pushed past the grid, a table or pivot range at
    or after the point, a range or spans item that does not parse, or a
    malformed col (P3 ruling 1). The comparison prints ONE line of counts and
    yes/no flags and no reference, value, text, name or part name. --plant
    <flag> changes the output as read so that the named flag turns to no; the
    line then says planted=yes, or planted=no when the pair gives the plant
    nothing to change.
    """
    import posixpath
    import re
    import sys
    import xml.etree.ElementTree as ET
    import zipfile
    
    MAIN = ("http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/spreadsheetml/2006/main",
            "http://purl.oclc.org/ooxml/spreadsheetml/main")
    RELS = "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/package/2006/relationships"
    ATTR = ("http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships",
            "http://purl.oclc.org/ooxml/officeDocument/relationships")
    
    def local(tag):
        if tag.startswith("{"):
            ns, _, name = tag[1:].partition("}")
            return ns, name
        return "", tag
    
    
    def named(element, prefix):
        """element with prefix put before every element name in it."""
        return re.sub(rb"<(/?)([A-Za-z])", lambda m: b"<" + m.group(1) + prefix + m.group(2), element)
    
    
    def rels_name(part):
        d, base = posixpath.split(part)
        return posixpath.join(d, "_rels", base + ".rels") if base else "_rels/.rels"
    
    
    def rels_of(z, part):
        name = rels_name(part)
        if name not in z.namelist():
            return []
        out = []
        for el in ET.fromstring(z.read(name)).iter("{%s}Relationship" % RELS):
            if el.get("TargetMode") == "External":
                continue
            target = el.get("Target", "")
            resolved = (target[1:] if target.startswith("/")
                        else posixpath.normpath(posixpath.join(posixpath.dirname(part), target)))
            out.append((el.get("Id"), el.get("Type", ""), resolved))
        return out
    
    
    def pick(z):
        """The first worksheet part in <sheets> order."""
        office = [t for (_, ty, t) in rels_of(z, "") if ty.endswith("/officeDocument")]
        if len(office) != 1:
            return None
        workbook = office[0]
        by_id = {i: (ty, t) for (i, ty, t) in rels_of(z, workbook)}
        for el in ET.fromstring(z.read(workbook)).iter():
            ns, name = local(el.tag)
            if ns in MAIN and name == "sheet":
                rid = next((el.get("{%s}id" % a) for a in ATTR if el.get("{%s}id" % a)), None)
                ty, target = by_id.get(rid, ("", None))
                if ty.endswith("/worksheet") and target in z.namelist():
                    return target
        return None
    
    
    TOKEN = re.compile(rb"<!--.*?-->|<[!?][^>]*>|<(/?)[^>]*?(/?)>", re.S)
    
    
    def top_level(data):
        """One (start, end) span per top-level element of some bytes."""
        spans = []
        depth = 0
        at = 0
        for m in TOKEN.finditer(data):
            tok = m.group(0)
            if tok.startswith(b"<!") or tok.startswith(b"<?"):
                continue
            if m.group(1):
                depth -= 1
                if depth == 0:
                    spans.append((at, m.end()))
            elif m.group(2):
                if depth == 0:
                    spans.append((m.start(), m.end()))
            else:
                if depth == 0:
                    at = m.start()
                depth += 1
        return spans
    
    
    def qname(raw):
        return re.match(rb"<([^\s/>]+)", raw).group(1)
    
    
    def split_name(q):
        p, _, n = q.rpartition(b":")
        return (p + b":" if p else b""), n.decode()
    
    
    def start_tag(raw):
        return raw[:raw.find(b">") + 1]
    
    
    def is_empty(raw):
        tag = start_tag(raw)
        return tag.endswith(b"/>")
    
    
    def inner(raw):
        """(offset of the content, offset of its end) in an element's bytes."""
        tag = start_tag(raw)
        if tag.endswith(b"/>"):
            return len(tag), len(tag)
        return len(tag), raw.rfind(b"</")
    
    
    def opened(tag):
        slash = tag.rfind(b"/")
        return tag[:slash] + tag[slash + 1:]
    
    
    ATTR_RE = rb'(?<=[\s])%s\s*=\s*("[^"]*"|\'[^\']*\')'
    
    
    def attributes(tag):
        """(name, value) of every attribute of a start tag, in order."""
        return [(m.group(1).decode(), m.group(3)[1:-1].decode())
                for m in re.finditer(rb'\s([^\s=/>]+)\s*=\s*(("[^"]*")|(\'[^\']*\'))', tag)]
    
    
    def with_attr(tag, name, value):
        """The unprefixed attribute set: replaced between its quotes, else put
        after the last attribute's closing quote, else after the name."""
        m = re.search(ATTR_RE % re.escape(name), tag)
        if m:
            q = m.start(1)
            return tag[:q + 1] + value + tag[m.end(1) - 1:]
        last = None
        for last in re.finditer(rb'\s[^\s=/>]+\s*=\s*("[^"]*"|\'[^\']*\')', tag):
            pass
        at = last.end() if last else len(re.match(rb"<[^\s/>]+", tag).group(0))
        return tag[:at] + b" " + name + b'="' + value + b'"' + tag[at:]
    
    
    def attr_value(tag, name):
        m = re.search(ATTR_RE % re.escape(name), tag)
        return m.group(1)[1:-1] if m else None
    
    
    def root_span(data):
        """(start of the root's content, end of it) and the root's prefix."""
        m = None
        for m in re.finditer(rb"<([^\s/>?!]+)", data):
            break
        close = data.find(b">", m.start())
        if data[close - 1:close] == b"/":
            return close + 1, close + 1, split_name(m.group(1))[0]
        end = data.rfind(b"</")
        return close + 1, end, split_name(m.group(1))[0]
    
    
    def children(data, a, b, root_prefix):
        """[(start, end, main local name or None)] of the root's children."""
        out = []
        for (x, y) in top_level(data[a:b]):
            p, n = split_name(qname(data[a + x:a + y]))
            out.append((a + x, a + y, n if p == root_prefix else None))
        return out
    
    
    def cut(data, spans):
        parts, at = [], 0
        for (x, y) in sorted(spans):
            parts.append(data[at:x])
            at = y
        parts.append(data[at:])
        return b"".join(parts)
    
    
    
    GRID_ROWS = 1048576
    GRID_COLUMNS = 16384
    LISTS = ("conditionalFormatting", "dataValidations", "hyperlinks", "autoFilter")
    NAMED_ROWS = ("sheetData", "dimension", "mergeCells") + LISTS
    NAMED_COLUMNS = NAMED_ROWS + ("cols",)
    FLAGS_ROWS = ("rest_same", "rows_before_same", "sheetdata_bytes", "cells_moved",
                  "dimension_ok", "merges_ok", "lists_ok", "calc_ok")
    FLAGS_COLUMNS = ("rest_same", "cells_before_same", "sheetdata_bytes", "cells_moved",
                     "spans_ok", "dimension_ok", "merges_ok", "cols_ok", "lists_ok", "calc_ok")
    DECIMAL_RE = re.compile(rb"(0|[1-9][0-9]*)")
    COMMENT = b"<!-- planted -->"
    A1_RE = re.compile(rb"^([A-Z]{1,7})([1-9][0-9]*)$")
    
    
    class Refused(Exception):
        pass
    
    
    def ref_parse(text):
        """(row, col) of an A1 reference, or None."""
        m = A1_RE.match(text)
        if not m:
            return None
        col = 0
        for ch in m.group(1):
            col = col * 26 + (ch - 64)
        return int(m.group(2)), col
    
    
    def a1(row, col):
        name = ""
        while col > 0:
            col, rest = divmod(col - 1, 26)
            name = chr(65 + rest) + name
        return "%s%d" % (name, row)
    
    
    def area_parse(text):
        """((r1, c1), (r2, c2)) normalised, or None."""
        halves = text.split(b":")
        if len(halves) > 2:
            return None
        a = ref_parse(halves[0])
        b = ref_parse(halves[1]) if len(halves) == 2 else a
        if a is None or b is None:
            return None
        return (min(a[0], b[0]), min(a[1], b[1])), (max(a[0], b[0]), max(a[1], b[1]))
    
    
    def area_a1(area):
        (r1, c1), (r2, c2) = area
        return (a1(r1, c1) if (r1, c1) == (r2, c2) else a1(r1, c1) + ":" + a1(r2, c2)).encode()
    
    
    def decimal(text):
        """The library's decimal u32: digits, no leading zero, below 2^32."""
        if DECIMAL_RE.fullmatch(text) is None or int(text) >= 1 << 32:
            return None
        return int(text)
    
    
    class Rule:
        def __init__(self, insert, k, n, columns=False):
            self.insert, self.k, self.n, self.columns = insert, k, n, columns
            self.limit = GRID_COLUMNS if columns else GRID_ROWS
    
        def on_axis(self, cell):
            """A (row, col) cell's index on the rule's axis."""
            return cell[1] if self.columns else cell[0]
    
        def index(self, i):
            if i < self.k:
                return i
            if self.insert:
                return i + self.n
            if i < self.k + self.n:
                return None
            return i - self.n
    
        def interval(self, a, b):
            """("whole"|"changed", a, b) or ("gone",)."""
            k, n = self.k, self.n
            if b < k:
                return ("whole", a, b)
            if self.insert:
                return ("whole", a + n, b + n) if a >= k else ("changed", a, b + n)
            last = k + n - 1
            if a > last:
                return ("whole", a - n, b - n)
            if a >= k and b <= last:
                return ("gone",)
            return ("changed", a if a < k else k, b - n if b > last else k - 1)
    
        def interval_clipped(self, a, b):
            """[a, b] through the rule and the clip, or None when removed or
            moved wholly past the grid."""
            got = self.interval(a, b)
            if got[0] == "gone" or got[1] > self.limit:
                return None
            return got[1], min(got[2], self.limit)
    
        def clipped(self, area):
            (r1, c1), (r2, c2) = area
            if self.columns:
                got = self.interval_clipped(c1, c2)
                return None if got is None else ((r1, got[0]), (r2, got[1]))
            got = self.interval_clipped(r1, r2)
            return None if got is None else ((got[0], c1), (got[1], c2))
    
    
    def moved_list(value, rule):
        """The list through the rule: None when it empties; the input's bytes
        when nothing changed; else single spaces, unchanged ranges as written."""
        kept, changed = [], False
        for rng in value.split():
            area = area_parse(rng)
            if area is None:
                raise Refused()
            got = rule.clipped(area)
            if got == area:
                kept.append(rng)
            elif got is None:
                changed = True
            else:
                changed = True
                kept.append(area_a1(got))
        if not kept:
            return None
        return b" ".join(kept) if changed else value
    
    
    def list_element(el, name, rule):
        """An element whose attribute name is a list, through the rule, or
        None when the list empties."""
        tag = start_tag(el)
        value = attr_value(tag, name)
        if value is None:
            return el
        got = moved_list(value, rule)
        if got is None:
            return None
        if got == value:
            return el
        return with_attr(tag, name, got) + el[len(tag):]
    
    
    def counted(el, child, rule, per_child):
        """A counted container through the rule: its children run through
        per_child, dropped ones cut, count its kept children; None when none is
        kept. One with no content is copied as it is."""
        if is_empty(el):
            return el
        a, b = inner(el)
        content = el[a:b]
        parts, at, kept = [], 0, 0
        for (x, y) in top_level(content):
            parts.append(content[at:x])
            c = content[x:y]
            at = y
            if split_name(qname(c))[1] == child:
                got = per_child(c)
                if got is None:
                    continue
                kept += 1
                parts.append(got)
            else:
                parts.append(c)
        parts.append(content[at:])
        if kept == 0:
            return None
        return with_attr(start_tag(el), b"count", str(kept).encode()) + b"".join(parts) + el[b:]
    
    
    def merge_child(c, rule):
        tag = start_tag(c)
        value = attr_value(tag, b"ref")
        if value is None:
            return c
        area = area_parse(value)
        if area is None:
            raise Refused()
        got = rule.clipped(area)
        if got == area:
            return c
        if got is None or got[0] == got[1]:
            return None
        return with_attr(tag, b"ref", area_a1(got)) + c[len(tag):]
    
    
    def moved_formula(tag, rule, dropping):
        t = attr_value(tag, b"t")
        if t not in (b"shared", b"array", b"dataTable"):
            return tag
        value = attr_value(tag, b"ref")
        if value is None:
            return tag
        area = area_parse(value)
        if area is None:
            raise Refused()
        first, last = rule.on_axis(area[0]), rule.on_axis(area[1])
        got = rule.interval(first, last)
        if got[0] == "gone":
            return tag
        if got[0] == "changed" or dropping or got[2] > rule.limit:
            raise Refused()
        if got[1] == first:
            return tag
        if rule.columns:
            moved = ((area[0][0], got[1]), (area[1][0], got[2]))
        else:
            moved = ((got[1], area[0][1]), (got[2], area[1][1]))
        return with_attr(tag, b"ref", area_a1(moved))
    
    
    def without_attr(tag, name):
        """The unprefixed attribute and the whitespace before it cut out; the
        tag as it is when it has none."""
        m = re.search(ATTR_RE % re.escape(name), tag)
        if m is None:
            return tag
        at = m.start()
        while at > 0 and tag[at - 1:at] in (b" ", b"\t", b"\n", b"\r"):
            at -= 1
        return tag[:at] + tag[m.end():]
    
    
    def moved_spans(tag, rule):
        """A row's start tag with its spans through the column rule (P3 ruling
        2)."""
        value = attr_value(tag, b"spans")
        if value is None:
            return tag
        kept, changed = [], False
        for item in re.split(rb"[ \t\n\r]+", value):
            if not item:
                continue
            a_text, colon, b_text = item.partition(b":")
            a, b = decimal(a_text), decimal(b_text)
            if not colon or a is None or b is None or a < 1 or a > b:
                raise Refused()
            got = rule.interval_clipped(a, b)
            if got == (a, b):
                kept.append(item)
            elif got is None:
                changed = True
            else:
                changed = True
                kept.append(b"%d:%d" % got)
        if not changed:
            return tag
        if not kept:
            return without_attr(tag, b"spans")
        return with_attr(tag, b"spans", b" ".join(kept))
    
    
    def moved_col(c, rule):
        """A col through the column rule: None when removed or moved wholly past
        the grid; a malformed min or max refused (P3 ruling 1)."""
        tag = start_tag(c)
        lo_text, hi_text = attr_value(tag, b"min"), attr_value(tag, b"max")
        lo = decimal(lo_text) if lo_text is not None else None
        hi = decimal(hi_text) if hi_text is not None else None
        if lo is None or hi is None or lo == 0 or lo > hi:
            raise Refused()
        got = rule.interval_clipped(lo, hi)
        if got is None:
            return None
        if got == (lo, hi):
            return c
        tag2 = with_attr(with_attr(tag, b"min", str(got[0]).encode()), b"max", str(got[1]).encode())
        return tag2 + c[len(tag):]
    
    
    def dropping_container(el, child, per_child):
        """A container streamed under the rule (hyperlinks, cols): children
        named child run through per_child and a dropped one cut, every other
        byte kept; None when no child is kept; one with no content copied as it
        is."""
        if is_empty(el):
            return el
        ia, ib = inner(el)
        content = el[ia:ib]
        parts, at, kept = [], 0, 0
        for (hx, hy) in top_level(content):
            parts.append(content[at:hx])
            at = hy
            h = content[hx:hy]
            if split_name(qname(h))[1] != child:
                parts.append(h)
                continue
            got = per_child(h)
            if got is not None:
                kept += 1
                parts.append(got)
        parts.append(content[at:])
        return el[:ia] + b"".join(parts) + el[ib:] if kept else None
    
    
    def expected_sheetdata(raw, rule):
        """sheetData through the rule, and whether a formula sits at or after
        k."""
        a, b = inner(raw)
        content = raw[a:b]
        parts, at, reaches = [], 0, False
        for (x, y) in top_level(content):
            parts.append(content[at:x])
            at = y
            row = content[x:y]
            if split_name(qname(row))[1] != "row":
                parts.append(row)
                continue
            rtag = start_tag(row)
            r = int(attr_value(rtag, b"r"))
            if rule.columns:
                to = r
                rtag = moved_spans(rtag, rule)
            else:
                to = rule.index(r)
            dropping = to is None
            if not rule.columns and not dropping and to > rule.limit:
                raise Refused()
            ra, rb = inner(row)
            rc = row[ra:rb]
            rparts, rat = [], 0
            for (cx, cy) in top_level(rc):
                rparts.append(rc[rat:cx])
                rat = cy
                cell = rc[cx:cy]
                if split_name(qname(cell))[1] != "c":
                    rparts.append(cell)
                    continue
                ctag = start_tag(cell)
                row_col = ref_parse(attr_value(ctag, b"r"))
                cell_dropping = dropping
                if rule.columns:
                    cto = rule.index(row_col[1])
                    cell_dropping = cto is None
                    if cto is not None and cto > rule.limit:
                        raise Refused()
                    if cto is not None and cto != row_col[1]:
                        ctag = with_attr(ctag, b"r", a1(r, cto).encode())
                elif to is not None and to != r:
                    ctag = with_attr(ctag, b"r", a1(to, row_col[1]).encode())
                ca, cb = inner(cell)
                cc = cell[ca:cb]
                cparts, cat = [], 0
                for (fx, fy) in top_level(cc):
                    cparts.append(cc[cat:fx])
                    cat = fy
                    f = cc[fx:fy]
                    if split_name(qname(f))[1] == "f":
                        if rule.on_axis(row_col) >= rule.k:
                            reaches = True
                        ft = start_tag(f)
                        f = moved_formula(ft, rule, cell_dropping) + f[len(ft):]
                    cparts.append(f)
                cparts.append(cc[cat:])
                if cell_dropping and rule.columns:
                    continue
                rparts.append(ctag if is_empty(cell) else ctag + b"".join(cparts) + cell[cb:])
            rparts.append(rc[rat:])
            if dropping:
                continue
            if to != r:
                rtag = with_attr(rtag, b"r", str(to).encode())
            parts.append(rtag if is_empty(row) else rtag + b"".join(rparts) + row[rb:])
        parts.append(content[at:])
        if is_empty(raw):
            return raw, reaches
        return raw[:a] + b"".join(parts) + raw[b:], reaches
    
    
    def table_top(z, part, columns):
        """T (U on the column axis): the largest last row (column) of W's table
        and pivot ranges; raises Refused for a range that does not parse or a
        part that is not there, as the library refuses both (P2 ruling 2)."""
        top = 0
        for (_, ty, target) in rels_of(z, part):
            location = ty.endswith("/pivotTable")
            if not (location or ty.endswith("/table")):
                continue
            if target not in z.namelist():
                raise Refused()
            root = ET.fromstring(z.read(target))
            el = root
            if location:
                el = next((e for e in root.iter() if local(e.tag)[1] == "location"), None)
            value = el.get("ref") if el is not None else None
            area = area_parse(value.encode()) if value else None
            if area is None:
                raise Refused()
            top = max(top, area[1][1] if columns else area[1][0])
        return top
    
    
    def model(din, rule):
        """{root child name: [expected element bytes or None]} for the named
        children, the sheetData bytes, and whether a formula reaches k."""
        a, b, rp = root_span(din)
        out = {}
        reaches = False
        for (x, y, n) in children(din, a, b, rp):
            el = din[x:y]
            if n == "sheetData" and "sheetData" not in out:
                got, reaches = expected_sheetdata(el, rule)
            elif n == "dimension":
                value = attr_value(start_tag(el), b"ref")
                area = area_parse(value) if value is not None else None
                if value is not None and area is None:
                    raise Refused()
                got = el
                if area is not None:
                    moved = rule.clipped(area)
                    if moved is None:
                        got = with_attr(start_tag(el), b"ref", b"A1") + el[len(start_tag(el)):]
                    elif moved != area:
                        got = with_attr(start_tag(el), b"ref", area_a1(moved)) + el[len(start_tag(el)):]
            elif n == "mergeCells":
                got = counted(el, "mergeCell", rule, lambda c: merge_child(c, rule))
            elif n == "dataValidations":
                got = counted(el, "dataValidation", rule, lambda c: list_element(c, b"sqref", rule))
            elif n == "hyperlinks":
                got = dropping_container(el, "hyperlink", lambda h: list_element(h, b"ref", rule))
            elif n == "cols" and rule.columns:
                got = dropping_container(el, "col", lambda c: moved_col(c, rule))
            elif n == "conditionalFormatting":
                got = list_element(el, b"sqref", rule)
            elif n == "autoFilter":
                got = list_element(el, b"ref", rule)
            else:
                continue
            out.setdefault(n, []).append(got)
        return out, reaches
    
    
    def calc_state(z):
        """(fullCalcOnLoad is 1 or true, a calcChain relationship exists)."""
        office = [t for (_, ty, t) in rels_of(z, "") if ty.endswith("/officeDocument")]
        wb = office[0]
        full = False
        for el in ET.fromstring(z.read(wb)).iter():
            if local(el.tag)[1] == "calcPr":
                full = el.get("fullCalcOnLoad") in ("1", "true")
                break
        chain = any(ty.endswith("/calcChain") for (_, ty, _) in rels_of(z, wb))
        return full, chain
    
    
    def cell_map(data):
        out = {}
        for el in ET.fromstring(data).iter():
            ns, name = local(el.tag)
            if ns in MAIN and name == "c":
                f = v = None
                for child in el:
                    cns, cname = local(child.tag)
                    if cns in MAIN and cname == "f":
                        f = (child.get("t"), child.text, child.get("si"))
                    elif cns in MAIN and cname in ("v", "is"):
                        v = ET.tostring(child)
                out[el.get("r")] = (el.get("s"), el.get("t"), f, v)
        return out
    
    
    def sheet_rows(sd):
        """[(row start tag, [(col, cell bytes)])] of a sheetData element."""
        out = []
        if is_empty(sd):
            return out
        a, b = inner(sd)
        content = sd[a:b]
        for (x, y) in top_level(content):
            row = content[x:y]
            if split_name(qname(row))[1] != "row":
                continue
            cells = []
            if not is_empty(row):
                ra, rb = inner(row)
                rc = row[ra:rb]
                for (cx, cy) in top_level(rc):
                    cell = rc[cx:cy]
                    if split_name(qname(cell))[1] != "c":
                        continue
                    cells.append((ref_parse(attr_value(start_tag(cell), b"r"))[1], cell))
            out.append((start_tag(row), cells))
        return out
    
    
    def plant(dout, flag, k):
        a, b, rp = root_span(dout)
        kids = children(dout, a, b, rp)
        first = {}
        for (x, y, n) in kids:
            first.setdefault(n, (x, y))
        if flag == "rest_same":
            return dout[:a] + COMMENT + dout[a:], True
        if flag in ("rows_before_same", "sheetdata_bytes", "cells_moved",
                    "cells_before_same", "spans_ok"):
            if "sheetData" not in first:
                return dout, False
            x, y = first["sheetData"]
            el = dout[x:y]
            ia, ib = inner(el)
            if flag == "rows_before_same":
                if ia == ib:
                    return dout, False
                return dout[:x + ia] + COMMENT + dout[x + ia:], True
            if flag == "sheetdata_bytes":
                m = re.search(rb'(<(?:\w+:)?c\b[^>]*?)\s*/?>', el)
                if m is None:
                    return dout, False
                t = m.group(0)
                w = t.replace(b' r="', b'  r="', 1)
                return dout[:x + m.start()] + w + dout[x + m.end():], w != t
            if flag == "cells_before_same":
                # The first cell left of the point, one space doubled in its tag.
                for m in re.finditer(rb'<(?:\w+:)?c\b[^>]*?\sr="([A-Z]+)[0-9]+"[^>]*>', el):
                    if ref_parse(m.group(1) + b"1")[1] < k:
                        t = m.group(0)
                        w = t.replace(b' r="', b'  r="', 1)
                        return dout[:x + m.start()] + w + dout[x + m.end():], w != t
                return dout, False
            if flag == "spans_ok":
                m = re.search(rb'<(?:\w+:)?row\b[^>]*>', el)
                if m is None:
                    return dout, False
                t = m.group(0)
                w = t.replace(b' r="', b'  r="', 1)
                return dout[:x + m.start()] + w + dout[x + m.end():], w != t
            m = re.search(rb"<(\w+:)?v>([^<]*)</", el)
            if m is None:
                return dout, False
            return dout[:x + m.start(2)] + b"123456789" + dout[x + m.end(2):], True
        if flag == "dimension_ok":
            if "dimension" not in first:
                return dout, False
            x, y = first["dimension"]
            el = dout[x:y]
            w = with_attr(start_tag(el), b"ref", b"ZZ1") + el[len(start_tag(el)):]
            return dout[:x] + w + dout[y:], True
        if flag in ("merges_ok", "cols_ok"):
            name = "mergeCells" if flag == "merges_ok" else "cols"
            if name not in first:
                return dout, False
            x, y = first[name]
            return dout[:x] + dout[y:], True
        if flag == "calc_ok":
            # Applied in main, to the workbook part as read.
            return dout, True
        if flag == "lists_ok":
            for n in LISTS:
                if n in first:
                    x, y = first[n]
                    return dout[:x] + dout[y:], True
            return dout, False
        return dout, False
    
    
    MODES = {"insert": (True, False), "delete": (False, False),
             "insert-columns": (True, True), "delete-columns": (False, True)}
    
    
    def main():
        args = sys.argv[1:]
        mode = args[0]
        if mode not in MODES:
            print("error=unknown-mode")
            return
        rule_insert, columns = MODES[mode]
        flags_all = FLAGS_COLUMNS if columns else FLAGS_ROWS
        named_all = NAMED_COLUMNS if columns else NAMED_ROWS
        zin = zipfile.ZipFile(args[1])
        part = pick(zin)
        if args[2:3] == ["--parts"]:
            # W, the workbook part, its rels part and its chain part (empty when
            # there is none), one per line, for the log to compare with the
            # runner's rows without printing them.
            office = [t for (_, ty, t) in rels_of(zin, "") if ty.endswith("/officeDocument")]
            wb = office[0] if office else ""
            chain = [t for (_, ty, t) in rels_of(zin, wb) if ty.endswith("/calcChain")] if wb else []
            print(part or "")
            print(wb)
            print(rels_name(wb) if wb else "")
            print(chain[0] if chain else "")
            return
        if part is None:
            print("found=0")
            return
        din = zin.read(part)
        try:
            k = max(2, table_top(zin, part, columns) + 1)
        except Refused:
            k = 2
            table_refused = True
        else:
            table_refused = False
        # The row samples insert two rows; the column samples one column; a
        # deletion takes one (specs/0018 "Harness runs", P3 ruling 3).
        rule = Rule(rule_insert, k, 2 if rule_insert and not columns else 1, columns)
        try:
            expected, reaches = model(din, rule)
            refuse = table_refused
        except Refused:
            expected, reaches, refuse = None, False, True
        if args[2:3] == ["--predict"]:
            print("refuse=%s" % ("yes" if refuse else "no"))
            return
        if args[2:3] == ["--unchanged"]:
            # Whether the model leaves W's bytes as they are: every element the
            # rule names comes out as the input's (P2 ruling 13).
            same = not refuse
            if same:
                a0, b0, rp0 = root_span(din)
                kids0 = children(din, a0, b0, rp0)
                for n in expected:
                    kept = [e for e in expected[n] if e is not None]
                    have = [din[x2:y2] for (x2, y2, n2) in kids0 if n2 == n]
                    if kept != have:
                        same = False
            print("unchanged=%s" % ("yes" if same else "no"))
            return
        planted_flag = args[args.index("--plant") + 1] if "--plant" in args else None
        if planted_flag is not None and planted_flag not in flags_all:
            print("error=unknown-plant")
            return
        if refuse:
            print("error=refused-input")
            return
        zout = zipfile.ZipFile(args[2])
        dout = zout.read(part)
        planted = True
        if planted_flag is not None:
            dout, planted = plant(dout, planted_flag, k)
        yn = lambda v: "yes" if v else "no"
        ai, bi, rp = root_span(din)
        ao, bo, rpo = root_span(dout)
        kin = children(din, ai, bi, rp)
        kout = children(dout, ao, bo, rpo)
        flags = {}
        flags["rest_same"] = (cut(din, [(x, y) for (x, y, n) in kin if n in named_all])
                              == cut(dout, [(x, y) for (x, y, n) in kout if n in named_all]))
        got = {}
        for (x, y, n) in kout:
            if n in named_all:
                got.setdefault(n, []).append(dout[x:y])
    
        def same(name):
            want = [e for e in expected.get(name, []) if e is not None]
            return got.get(name, []) == want
    
        sd_in = next(din[x:y] for (x, y, n) in kin if n == "sheetData")
        sd_out = got.get("sheetData", [b""])[0]
        if columns:
            rows_in = sheet_rows(sd_in)
            rows_out = sheet_rows(sd_out) if sd_out else []
            left_in = [c for (_, cells) in rows_in for (col, c) in cells if col < k]
            left_out = [c for (_, cells) in rows_out for (col, c) in cells if col < k]
            flags["cells_before_same"] = left_in == left_out
            want_sd = [e for e in expected.get("sheetData", []) if e is not None]
            want_tags = [t for (t, _) in sheet_rows(want_sd[0])] if want_sd else []
            flags["spans_ok"] = [t for (t, _) in rows_out] == want_tags
            flags["cols_ok"] = same("cols")
        else:
            ia, ib = inner(sd_in)
            oa, ob = inner(sd_out) if sd_out else (0, 0)
            first_at = ib
            for (x, y) in top_level(sd_in[ia:ib]):
                row = sd_in[ia + x:ia + y]
                if split_name(qname(row))[1] == "row" and int(attr_value(start_tag(row), b"r")) >= k:
                    first_at = ia + x
                    break
            prefix = sd_in[ia:first_at]
            flags["rows_before_same"] = sd_out[oa:oa + len(prefix)] == prefix and sd_out[:oa] == sd_in[:ia]
        flags["sheetdata_bytes"] = same("sheetData")
        cin, cout = cell_map(din), cell_map(dout)
        want_cells = {}
        for ref, tup in cin.items():
            row, col = ref_parse(ref.encode())
            to = rule.index(col if columns else row)
            if to is not None:
                want_cells[a1(row, to) if columns else a1(to, col)] = tup
        flags["cells_moved"] = cout == want_cells
        flags["dimension_ok"] = same("dimension")
        flags["merges_ok"] = same("mergeCells")
        flags["lists_ok"] = all(same(n) for n in LISTS)
        full_in, chain_in = calc_state(zin)
        full_out, chain_out = calc_state(zout)
        if planted_flag == "calc_ok":
            # The workbook part as read says the opposite about the flag.
            full_out = not full_out
        if reaches:
            flags["calc_ok"] = full_out and not chain_out
        else:
            flags["calc_ok"] = full_out == full_in and chain_out == chain_in
        moved_formulas = sum(1 for ref, tup in cin.items()
                             if tup[2] is not None and rule.on_axis(ref_parse(ref.encode())) >= k)
        fields = ["found=1", "planted=%s" % yn(planted), "at=%d" % k,
                  "cells_in=%d" % len(cin), "cells_out=%d" % len(cout),
                  "formulas_moved=%d" % moved_formulas,
                  "chain_in=%d" % chain_in, "chain_out=%d" % chain_out, "full_out=%d" % full_out]
        print(" ".join(fields + ["%s=%s" % (f, yn(flags[f])) for f in flags_all]))
    
    
    main()
